{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":1075,"cacheRead":53447,"cacheWrite":1787,"totalTokens":56311,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0005375,"cacheRead":0.00053447,"cacheWrite":0.000223375,"total":0.001295545,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":307},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Fixed. Flexible `ratio` columns now keep at least one visible character plus padding, and the ratio helpers no longer assert on edge cases.\n\n**Root cause**\n\n- Under a narrow console, the fixed columns (22 + 18 + padding) left only 2 cells for `Load`. Its minimum is 3 (1 content + 2 padding).\n- The collapse step then shrank `Load` to 2, which leaves zero content. The header and values vanish into `||`.\n- `ratio_distribute` asserted `total_ratio > 0`, so all-zero ratios (for example, an empty expanded table with a `min_width`) crashed.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- `rich/table.py`: after collapsing, flexible columns are raised back to their minimum. The space comes from the widest other columns. This only applies when the minimums fit in the available width, and only when a flexible column is actually below its minimum.\n- `rich/_ratio.py`: `ratio_distribute` no longer asserts. If all weights are zero, it splits the space equally. A negative total yields `[0, 0]` rather than negative widths.\n- Tests added in `tests/test_table.py` and `tests/test_tools.py`.\n\n**Results**\n\n- At width 50 the reproduction now renders `Load` as `… ` (one content cell plus padding) instead of vanishing. At 60 the output is unchanged.\n- The new width-50 regression test fails on the original code and passes now.\n- Fuzzing about 3000 ratio inputs and roughly 1300 table configurations (widths 0–69) produces no exceptions. Before the fix, the same fuzzer hit `AssertionError` in both `ratio_distribute` and table rendering.\n- Full suite: the same 12 failures as before my change (syntax, markdown, card; unrelated to tables). Nothing new fails.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- I didn't reproduce a `ZeroDivisionError`. The code paths I checked are already guarded, so I may not have hit the exact scenario from the report.\n- At very narrow widths where the minimums can't fit, the old behavior is kept. `test_render_table` pins that output.\n- `python`, `black` and `mypy` aren't on the PATH here. I ran with `python3` and `PYTHONPATH=/app`, and didn't run the formatters or the type checker."}}
